Programs selling "AI-powered" stores or done-for-you AI income are the newest version of this pattern, and the FTC has sued several of them. In September 2024, the agency announced [Operation AI Comply](https://www.ftc.gov/news-events/news/press-releases/2024/09/ftc-announces-crackdown-deceptive-ai-claims-schemes) to target schemes promoting bogus passive income. Among those targets, Ascend Ecom resulted in at least $25 million in alleged consumer losses after falsely promising fast five-figure monthly returns from automated storefronts. In 2025, the FTC sued Click Profit over alleged losses of at least $14 million, finding about 95% of its stores were blocked, suspended, or terminated by Amazon. Under the Business Opportunity Rule, any seller making an earnings claim must provide a written earnings claim statement showing the exact percentage of buyers who achieved those results. Ask for that document before paying anyone.